      "created_at": "2019-10-08T17:32:59Z",
      "updated_at": "2019-10-08T17:32:59Z",
      "body": "From Manuel:\r\nI got some info about how to implement it from the Telemetry team. They pointed out a couple of things though:\r\n- They were concern about sending a ping after the the user opts out, we need to really justify the need of this so we can pass the data review\r\n- It seems that some sort of user information is sent with the event ping so we will be able to group by user through backend queries\r\n- They told me that there is always a discrepancy between our telemetry and external sources and trying to hard to fill the gap might be a time sink and lead nowhere: “In general things never match with external data sources” (edited) ",
      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "pin": null,
